BEGIN {
    if ($ENV{REEXEC_LOOP}) {
        delete $ENV{REEXEC_LOOP};
    } elsif ($^O =~ /MSWin32/) {
        warn "Ignoring re-exec under Windows";
    } else {
        local $ENV{REEXEC_LOOP} = 1;
        exec($_, $0, @ARGV);
        die "Could not exec $_";
    }
}
__END__

Use like:
  #!/usr/bin/env perl
  do "./lib/reexec" for grep $_, $ENV{MY_CUSTOM_PATH};
at the head of a perl program.

Reinvokes this script with the same arguments using the perl provided by
the custom path (passed in as $_), with best-effort attempts to avoid
breakage.

Not currently supported under Windows, let me know if you want it: there
is probably a way to support it.
